          ><div class="i4z5KmU7MeczeayCD" data-instant-type="tabs-pane" id="4z5KmU7MeczeayCD"
            ><div class="iuapLorG0wczGDxrr" data-instant-type="accordion-container" data-is-first-open="true" data-is-multi-open-enabled="false"
              ><div data-state="open" class="iPthpANLUbF7xfNjE" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="i0fFg79KJlr5ueUAc" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text izRBxlOnK5ekNcEW3"><h3>What does it taste like?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iFrvKqYQoF4elu4lo">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="iLmrz0DueGXvl2LXn" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i1X3T5JSCIAMfycge"><p>If you&apos;re used to vapor, Lio may not be as strong as you&apos;d expect at first. Lio can be compared to a herbal tea if vapor was compared to a sticky soda. Not as sweet, and a lot more natural.</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="iv7a2xK9O3gKQ2naJ" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="ifcGhFfm0f89Casph" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i1V1J6e0ZsSzhiQNg"><h3>What is Lio?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iWF2d9Mc09wP0MqBn">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="ilPOfPkjUzZLBN0dk" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i9m983m0yqEzDwa3y"><p>Lio is a natural habit-breaking device that uses aromatherapy to help you manage cravings without nicotine, chemicals, or harmful additives. It works through olfactory conditioning, the science of how scent influences your brain and behavior.</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="iM76wMxtwjqbkdbrd" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="iLsiQbqOOel8iXFhr" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iMJERnJV1p7IwYOMo"><h3>How does Lio work?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="ikeuLj7kh8Z8FkefX">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="iSUCPbYs1A1u0EW12" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iDcM12g5BgzvwSQUf"><p>Stopping a bad habit cold turkey is extremely hard on your brain. Lio helps by replacing your hand-to-mouth fixation, encouraging calming breaths that reduce stress, activating scent receptors that interrupt habit pathways, and providing immediate sensory satisfaction with natural aromatherapy. You&apos;re breathing nothing but clean air infused with natural plant aromatics, no nicotine, no chemicals, no vapor.</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="iwhKtizPPEGMg32cU" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="iqu5DGQEuhYgg8sfE" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iEfgIsLw7rVwyZpmT"><h3>How can something with no nicotine actually work?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iruCLYKfrbWDdaKlU">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="iFcFD9ap3UWOKfl1E" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iyRM3J5CsyivOgmjz"><p>Here&apos;s what most people don&apos;t know: addiction isn&apos;t just about the chemical substance. Science shows it&apos;s ritual plus chemical. The hand-to-mouth motion, the deep breathing, the sensory triggers, these behavioral patterns create 50-70% of the addiction. Lio targets this ritual component. Your brain doesn&apos;t just crave the substance, it craves the entire experience. That&apos;s why customers say it "works like magic" even without nicotine.</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="iFbAcuqVgZlLASl06" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="ivF1DuO2AP74xDIrW" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iplqQNy7pzrz2EpUT"><h3>This looks like another wellness gimmick. Is it really different?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="ihoVlLspVSeX5UyO5">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="iQN0Bn17RJx9abg1X" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iAWAVzMjHyekbGjaB"><p>Lio isn&apos;t based on Instagram trends. It&apos;s grounded in established research on olfactory conditioning and behavioral psychology. We use pharmaceutical-grade aromatics from IFRA-certified EU farms, have multiple 3rd party toxicology reports, and have helped 100,000+ customers across 50+ countries achieve real results. Our devices are produced in the Netherlands with medical-grade materials. This is a clinical tool based on sensory science, not a lifestyle accessory.</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="ipEmqMmceKay95bqT" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="in9hU7r85azbjuw98" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iI5RNA23gKr1wtLhv"><h3>Will this actually satisfy my cravings?</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="irtaV1wEX8YB7tYKv">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                      <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                    </svg></div></button
                ><div class="iZLQryEjsgb0Nc9uj" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iqIDkysHg7mDZzrtL"><p>Yes. Lio mimics the physical sensations you&apos;re craving: the throat hit from menthol blends, the hand-to-mouth ritual, the stress relief from deep breathing, and the immediate sensory reward. You&apos;re not white-knuckling through cravings, you&apos;re satisfying them in a healthier way. As one customer said: "It gives the throat feeling like a cig without the harm."</p></div></div
                ></div
              ><div data-state="closed" class="ijTwSXUdDIpp0oS8e" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
                ><button class="iHOtqYn53Wg42c0ZZ" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
